const e={"seo.purpose":"What this character worksheet is for","seo.purpose.p1":"Paste a lesson, a character list or a string of Chinese characters, and the tool looks up the zhuyin, radical and stroke count of each one and lays them out as a printable A4 practice sheet. Parents no longer have to draw tables in Word, and teachers can add a sheet for a class at short notice.","seo.purpose.p2":"It is used for early primary school character practice, review sheets at after-school classes, practising zhuyin with a child at home, and for drilling just the few characters in a name or a new vocabulary word.","seo.why":"Why use this worksheet","seo.why.p1":"Readings, radicals and stroke counts come from the Ministry of Education's Concised Dictionary and the CNS11643 character bank, so nothing has to be looked up by hand and a copied mistake cannot be taught.","seo.why.li1":"Fix polyphonic characters yourself: a character can be read differently from word to word, and one click on a reading updates both the preview and the printout.","seo.why.li2":"Choose the grid: cross grid, star grid or blank, with adjustable text size and practice boxes, all fitted to one A4 page.","seo.why.li3":'Ready to write on: the header leaves room for a name and a date, and "Save as PDF" keeps a copy you can print again.',"seo.why.p2":"The whole worksheet is generated in your browser. Nothing you paste is uploaded, and there is no account and nothing to install.","seo.faq":"Worksheet questions","seo.faq.q1":"Does the printout include zhuyin?","seo.faq.q1a":"Yes. The example box of every character prints its zhuyin, and the character list also shows the radical and stroke count.","seo.faq.q2":"What about characters with several readings?","seo.faq.q2a":"Click the reading in the character list and choose another one; the preview and the printout update straight away.","seo.faq.q3":"Can I use my own font?","seo.faq.q3a":"The font setting offers three Kai stacks. Which font actually appears depends on the Kai fonts installed on your computer.","seo.faq.q4":"Why is a character missing?","seo.faq.q4a":"The table covers 4,808 common characters, so rare, variant or simplified forms may be missing. The tool lists them; try the common form instead.","seo.faq.q5":"Can I save the worksheet as a PDF?","seo.faq.q5a":'Yes. Press "Print / save as PDF" and set the destination to "Save as PDF" in the browser print dialog.',"seo.faq.q6":"How many characters fit on one sheet?","seo.faq.q6a":"Up to {max} characters per sheet (repeats included); anything beyond that is reported so you can print in batches."};export{e as default};
//# sourceMappingURL=worksheet-DF4AyDsH.js.map
